From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wbemprox: IClientSecurity, IWbemContext, qualifier sets, class derivation and WQL string escapes

Ground truth from Wine's wbemprox tests (todo_wine marks removed: IClientSecurity reference counts, IWbemContext enumeration, ProcessId of a failed Win32_Process.Create reading as NULL, LIKE "PCI\%" being an invalid query, \\ROOT being an unreachable machine).

IClientSecurity is another interface of the object it was queried from and shares its count; SetBlanket values come back from QueryBlanket. IWbemContext: GetNames, BeginEnumeration/Next/EndEnumeration, DeleteValue, DeleteAll. IWbemQualifierSet is a real set (Get/Put/Delete/GetNames/enumeration, implied [key] [CIMTYPE] [implemented] [dynamic]). Class derivation (__DERIVATION, __SUPERCLASS, __DYNASTY, InheritsFrom), GetPropertyOrigin/GetMethodOrigin, Clone, CompareTo, Delete, PutMethod/DeleteMethod errors, GetNames with qualifier and key/ref/origin flags, IEnumWbemClassObject::NextAsync. WQL strings are unescaped (backslash escapes backslash and quotes); property values that are text (DeviceID, file names) now hold the real value and are escaped in paths and object text. DllCanUnloadNow and LockServer count live objects. __SystemSecurity SetSD stores the descriptor (administrators only) and GetSD returns it.
